[medium] collector.go:294 (correctness)
ListSecrets is called without IncludePlannedDeletion, and the AWS SDK documents that secrets scheduled for deletion are excluded by default. That makes this collector silently skip exactly the records where config.deleted_date and the CloudTrail-derived recovery_window_days would matter, so deletion/recovery policies cannot evaluate pending-deletion secrets.
Suggested fix: Set IncludePlannedDeletion: aws.Bool(true) on every ListSecrets request and add a collector test that verifies a scheduled-deletion secret is included and can receive DeleteSecret recovery_window_days enrichment.
Guidance: In collector.go, update listSecretARNs so every sm.ListSecretsInput includes IncludePlannedDeletion: aws.Bool(true) along with NextToken. Do not try to infer deleted secrets from CloudTrail alone; the collector must list scheduled-deletion secrets so collectSecret can DescribeSecret them and newSecretRecord can expose config.deleted_date. Add/adjust a collector test using fakeSM.ListSecrets to assert the input flag is true on each paginated call, and include a DescribeSecretOutput with DeletedDate plus a DeleteSecret CloudTrail event whose requestParameters.recoveryWindowInDays enriches recovery_window_days.
