[medium] collector.go:273 (correctness)
IAM credential-removal events are looked up with the target region's CloudTrail client. IAM is a global service whose CloudTrail event history is surfaced in us-east-1, so targets collected only in another region can miss DeleteUser/DeleteAccessKey/DetachUserPolicy/RemoveUserFromGroup events and fail to attach the account-wide credential-removal evidence promised by the plugin design.
Suggested fix: Lookup iam.amazonaws.com events through a CloudTrail client configured for us-east-1 per account, then attach those events to secrets across that account's regional targets; cover a non-us-east-1 secret target in tests.
Guidance: In collector.go, keep Secrets Manager CloudTrail lookup using clients.CloudTrail for the target region, but perform the iam.amazonaws.com lookup with a CloudTrail client configured for us-east-1 for the same account credentials. A low-risk implementation is to add an IAM/global CloudTrail client to AWSClientSet or add a small helper in DefaultAWSClientFactory that copies target.Config, sets Region = "us-east-1", and creates cloudtrail.NewFromConfig from that copy; then collectTarget must pass that us-east-1 client only to lookupEvents for iamCredentialRemovalEventNames. Do not change attachIAMCredentialEvents behavior: IAM events still attach only when affectedIAMIdentifiers substring-match resource-policy principals, and unmatched IAM events stay dropped. Add a test with a target Region such as us-west-2 and separate fake CloudTrail clients so the IAM lookup is proven to use the us-east-1/global client while Secrets Manager events still use the regional client.

